    {
      "id": "e24c310ed4788559b3f561c96fda1be721f00703",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1970302471,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "A couple of observations:\n\n1. All the spectre mitigations have some performance aspect, I've observed this in the day job but not looked at Wireshark performance.  I do think it's better to be safe.\n2. Using the /Qspectre flag also requires the spectre mitigated libs to be available for linking.  This might need a change in the Dev Guide docs for VS installation.\n3. There are other spectre flags (Qspectre-jmp, Qspectre-load, Qspect-load-cf) available that have a bigger performance hit so their impact should be evaluated before pushing them into release builds.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8730bfac2267cb97ff1f8187d285f244745a03a783055c8fd6fcd679bfa71c6e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/graham.bloice"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-27T08:26:46.471Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-27T20:55:46.071Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 311257511,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 16165,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1971821375,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Prior to this change we tested for /Qspectre support twice, for both C and C++, and since we require VS 2019 those tests were always successful. This change short-circuits that. It looks like the \".Spectre\" components are [unaffiliated](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/install/workload-component-id-vs-community?view=vs-2022#unaffiliated-components), so it would probably make sense to note that in the Developer's Guide.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789689689",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-27T20:55:45.997Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-27T20:55:45.997Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 311257511,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 16165,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1971849017,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, OK. I had assumed that /QSpectre test would always succeed whether or not the mitigation libraries were installed, but that doesn't appear to be the case. I'll revert this change and update some comments and documentation.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1789689689",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-06-27T21:20:13.357Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-06-27T21:20:13.357Z",
